#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128784 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d3a0d58-20a3-570d-91e7-aa8f10dafb5a" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Triple Integral as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "5f6a3dd8-65fb-5e1f-aa19-d0115c9aa217" :question/math-academy-id "e-11585" :question/problem "Express the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\iiint\\limits_{R} (x+y+z)^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR = \\bigg\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0\\leq z \\leq 2 \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\int_a^b  \\int_c^d  \\int_e^f \\ldots \\: \\textrm{d}y\\:  \\textrm{d}z\\:  \\textrm{d}x .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+y+z)^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+y+z)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128789 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "ff5e1f9e-d67d-5264-b556-2f7b3a946c3f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12391" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R z-xy  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\:0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 1 \\leq z \\leq 3 \\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} z-xy \\: \\textrm{d}V\n= \n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{1}^{3} z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\textrm d V = \\textrm d z\\:\\textrm d x\\:\\textrm d y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}z-xy\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}z-xy\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}-xyz]}_{z=1}^{z=3}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(9-1)-xy(3-1)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2xy\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2xy\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2yx\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[4x-y{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}4(2-0)-y({2}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}8-4y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}8-4y\\,dy & =[8y-2{y}^{2}]_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =8(1-(-1))-2({1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2-2(1-1) \\\\  & =16-0 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128949 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "9a9885cc-6a93-57ee-bfd0-b4285395e326" :question/math-academy-id "e-7263" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\iiint\\limits_{R} y \\cos{x} \\sin{z} \\: \\textrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R = \\bigg\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\pi \\bigg\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R = \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right]\\times[0,1]\\times\\left[0,\\pi\\right]$ is a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4655f5-09c6-5a42-a710-a1ed3ff62bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340049} {:answer/id #uuid "4273271e-eb54-59f5-90dd-17df7e633b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340050} {:answer/id #uuid "a64abae2-897e-5c57-992b-857bbd3b84a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340051} {:answer/id #uuid "13f8f340-ef99-5b01-b909-f4bd3c745fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340052} {:answer/id #uuid "aa77bfdf-f61b-50d7-b3f6-b0e946ffbc98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a64abae2-897e-5c57-992b-857bbd3b84a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340051} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a54a42a-c42a-5da8-b8b4-f017587eb533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffd92837-16f0-58e8-90f2-50cab6f18326" :question/math-academy-id "q-161274" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}]\\times [0,1]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot y\\cdot {e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [{e}^{z}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{2}+2\\sqrt{2})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (5-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76a6e3b7-be0e-5c00-a7f1-02e859ebabcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340056} {:answer/id #uuid "12a32758-93a7-5d0b-b92c-a55e590f8a51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340057} {:answer/id #uuid "bafb1024-ca7d-5e5a-a3c3-b184fa2fd4f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340058} {:answer/id #uuid "eec24d78-a26b-5ecd-ad0c-a52c953dae2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340059} {:answer/id #uuid "7e30fb2f-f116-5950-bd5b-bc9b1fecd029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e30fb2f-f116-5950-bd5b-bc9b1fecd029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340060} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5475c6-7cd5-58a9-94ca-072db8213840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4bcb4a4c-0e47-5f89-9d6f-fb2414084daf" :question/math-academy-id "q-161277" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,1\\le z\\le e}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]\\times [-1,1]\\times [1,e]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =[{e}^{x}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot [y]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡z]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(3-1)\\cdot (1-(-1))\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d3a0d58-20a3-570d-91e7-aa8f10dafb5a" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Triple Integral as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042b27fb-7859-5d28-9282-bf72b899ee3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340063} {:answer/id #uuid "24732283-f3cd-53f7-b239-b36e98a46288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340064} {:answer/id #uuid "92f1c375-dd69-5782-ac2d-a5c2baf94fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340065} {:answer/id #uuid "480458c9-af0c-5887-addd-968d02085151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340066} {:answer/id #uuid "8657c936-f45c-5485-a7ae-a39dcb45a903" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8657c936-f45c-5485-a7ae-a39dcb45a903" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340067} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ef6cadd-9e4a-5a15-a6d7-4fcefa156130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2eec7c1e-5bc0-58bd-8226-fb581d3a8e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-161333" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nGiven that the triple integral above is considered over the rectangular box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a+b=1+4=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d3a0d58-20a3-570d-91e7-aa8f10dafb5a" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Triple Integral as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d61cdee-14ce-5180-b320-0ce83fa58156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340070} {:answer/id #uuid "e002b779-2d32-5855-ac28-715c46925c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340071} {:answer/id #uuid "a7cd5110-e6db-566b-aae0-1f0ab14b851a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340072} {:answer/id #uuid "60415c25-148f-5075-ade6-8e1bef3afb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340073} {:answer/id #uuid "300fbf6d-1a07-51ac-92e4-3889c2dddfd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60415c25-148f-5075-ade6-8e1bef3afb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340073} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cad5ad9-286f-593b-9b3c-15957943bdc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d474f03e-2bc0-5695-adf3-ce5e50d64699" :question/math-academy-id "q-161334" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz\n$$\n\nGiven that the triple integral above is considered over the rectangular box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le e,\\,1\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{e}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a+b=-2+3=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d3a0d58-20a3-570d-91e7-aa8f10dafb5a" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Triple Integral as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "396d048c-56c4-50c0-8fe2-18614578cac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340077} {:answer/id #uuid "2256324c-b54a-5a96-be0d-e4a80ee7bea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340078} {:answer/id #uuid "343e859f-73e0-5dec-9ce9-719b4e51824a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340079} {:answer/id #uuid "edabf4cf-97af-5fb3-ad01-2a5e89e4a827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340080} {:answer/id #uuid "0177b74c-6231-50d3-8a32-bbd5bdafea19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "396d048c-56c4-50c0-8fe2-18614578cac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340077} :answer-field/id #uuid "244e9340-e7a7-5d38-86ea-17bd7228460f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "825a1b17-7e35-53ff-bd30-0a045f2e4adc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161337" :question/problem "Express the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 5}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{e}^{f}…\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "486a304a-f0c0-5234-b436-b7e29645a622" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340084} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa51ae8-8eb7-5423-bda7-ef508a879243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340085} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a06a3d-80fe-580b-aa3c-3615383b7cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340086} {:answer/id #uuid "7376264d-155a-526b-8299-b998f407056a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340087} {:answer/id #uuid "8b103a97-96c7-50a2-84f2-712fde6f0734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaa51ae8-8eb7-5423-bda7-ef508a879243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340085} :answer-field/id #uuid "10c294d7-9fcc-5128-8bcf-121e7ee29776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "847d64e7-2eb3-57b2-be63-47be2fd1b2c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161356" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V,\\,\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le z\\le 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\times [\\frac{1}{2},1]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{z}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =(1+1)\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (-1+2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af13879c-123c-5d3f-afc6-6b860c11df89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340091} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe005e8-e412-5e51-af17-1d7402330107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340092} {:answer/id #uuid "2df85a58-bf76-5040-9a44-76181be3bbc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340093} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb2457e-5d8f-5ba6-b0c8-16ac3562e7c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340094} {:answer/id #uuid "b6de62d4-b532-500f-9402-0562d2b1978b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af13879c-123c-5d3f-afc6-6b860c11df89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340091} :answer-field/id #uuid "80c456ed-05b9-57f6-ab3e-40e1d7f5a918" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ba99aad-f767-577f-9f2e-4f1acdc0b667" :question/math-academy-id "q-161362" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}V,\\,\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,1\\le z\\le 3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[1,e]\\times [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot {y}^{2}\\cdot (z-1)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{3}(z-1)\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{3}(z-1)\\,\\text{d}z & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}-z]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (\\frac{8}{3}-0)\\cdot (\\frac{9}{2}-3-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc330589-524d-5f6d-abbd-d4bf55dc636f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340098} {:answer/id #uuid "6505f390-82b6-54ad-acca-ce330826a456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340099} {:answer/id #uuid "bd70535d-6a17-5dcb-a064-0d38d1759309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340100} {:answer/id #uuid "af700abf-e393-536c-84c6-28e9e2bdd2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340101} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e0965c-cca5-58de-b45e-5097922cedbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd70535d-6a17-5dcb-a064-0d38d1759309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340100} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f93ba53-6104-5737-b6a4-d6ef8a7a3658" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bcc2ee3c-b8b3-5347-927a-92abaeddb8ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-161366" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+xz]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(1-0)z\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+yz]}_{y=0}^{y=\\pi }\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}(0-0)+(\\pi -0)z\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\pi z\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\pi z\\,dz & =\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,dz \\\\  & =\\pi {[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d7c294-f298-52f6-aca0-628d6cdaf404" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340105} {:answer/id #uuid "9628597c-0eb5-5005-a9f5-e959c1a88fd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340106} {:answer/id #uuid "8d0d48d7-8d46-5e79-9bd7-4f6621391268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340107} {:answer/id #uuid "c9066ec9-568e-58c0-85a4-8d257cd6b523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340108} {:answer/id #uuid "819cb6d2-6e8e-5afb-9026-e4d0a5ea977f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "819cb6d2-6e8e-5afb-9026-e4d0a5ea977f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340109} :answer-field/id #uuid "efb8bb64-7ae6-58c0-8f5a-6014d97f4cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db9f942e-9a57-5139-b193-ca2a7bfc27e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161367" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x{y}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi }\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}-z(-1-1)+{y}^{2}(\\pi -0)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2z+\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2z+\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2z+\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{z}^{2}+\\pi {y}^{2}z]_{z=-1}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-1)+\\pi {y}^{2}(2-(-1))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3+3\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3+3\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dy & =[3y+\\pi {y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =3(1-0)+\\pi (1-0) \\\\  & =3+\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43a43bf8-c4b6-5b4c-a8f2-445f34d0127b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340112} {:answer/id #uuid "65d13d58-5134-5254-a138-e1985707f378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340113} {:answer/id #uuid "e12864db-ab59-563c-84e9-8d37d9f82844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340114} {:answer/id #uuid "7224824c-42ae-502c-af00-48e14031343c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3({e}^{2}-2e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340115} {:answer/id #uuid "25afcce9-9893-57c8-86b7-1ec85d21dc6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65d13d58-5134-5254-a138-e1985707f378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340113} :answer-field/id #uuid "09d17851-92ab-5039-bd21-fc020284d7a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa09d034-4318-5de0-b0e8-a01caa940832" :question/math-academy-id "q-161368" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z{e}^{x}+2xy]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}z({e}^{3}-1)+2(3-0)y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{3}-1)z+6y\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{3}-1)z+6y\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{3}-1)z+6y\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}\\,{z}^{2}+6yz]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}(1-0)+6y(1-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}+6y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}+6y\\,dy & ={[\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}\\,y+3{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}(1-(-1))+3(1-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dc8416c-d557-5cc2-88af-824c6d3e5e8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340119} {:answer/id #uuid "6a5589cc-3510-5058-8bf0-e2f792f77e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340120} {:answer/id #uuid "9559cd44-2370-59f9-8066-d02d9127e78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340121} {:answer/id #uuid "499a7c20-fdff-5fbb-9613-559a16bdd410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340122} {:answer/id #uuid "d5791df1-b711-5ff5-8b8e-aa30c72c1813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "499a7c20-fdff-5fbb-9613-559a16bdd410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340122} :answer-field/id #uuid "c18e9da6-c72f-516b-a5e3-49db3abd3fee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "96cc9b53-f4d3-5f3d-b1ed-d155cc070b3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161372" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}5x-3y\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-1\\le z\\le 0}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}5x-3y\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5x-3y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5x-3y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}5x-3y\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[5xy-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}5x(2-0)-\\frac{3}{2}(4-0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}10x-6\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}10x-6\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-1}^{0}10x-6\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(10x-6)z]_{z=-1}^{z=0}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(10x-6)(0-(-1))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10x-6\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}10x-6\\,dx & =[5{x}^{2}-6x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =5(1-0)-6(1-0) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5423789-1e08-5a57-9551-8ac6459cc9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126507} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf388d2-e394-5178-8740-8d5930578fa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126508} {:answer/id #uuid "dc46bf67-ff25-57c6-81da-fc7cc95cf285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(e^{2} - 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126509} {:answer/id #uuid "f95f9667-8a24-5ea6-b059-467599e685f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126510} {:answer/id #uuid "7012b9cb-9f58-5777-b6c9-98f70c788057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5423789-1e08-5a57-9551-8ac6459cc9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126507} :answer-field/id #uuid "7652d5fb-da25-50aa-81fe-e299053395cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ce80f42-293e-5e66-a70f-dd95799ecbec" :question/math-academy-id "q-161374" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\le z\\le 2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x-y){e}^{z}]_{z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{z=2}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)[\\frac{1}{2}(1-0)-(1-0)y]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy & =({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}-y\\,dy \\\\  & =({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-2}{2}(0-(-1)+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8da11700-fec0-5bc3-a000-ef6d8869ed80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127845} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2c85a1-440d-5a3e-8973-080c6fe40c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127846} {:answer/id #uuid "336b0d75-478d-51be-b6e4-c7a7a06faaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127847} {:answer/id #uuid "40170cf1-f81e-552e-adeb-a0ea3f961415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127848} {:answer/id #uuid "67ea7c30-f76f-520e-a761-1516d9a33ecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8da11700-fec0-5bc3-a000-ef6d8869ed80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127845} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fcfe628-79f8-5403-9aa4-4d36aab5a2a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8712bce7-9b2f-578f-98a6-ec22ffc6519a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39475" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}V,\\,\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z}\\cdot {e}^{y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}_{1}^{e}\\cdot {[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {[{e}^{z}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (3-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d3a0d58-20a3-570d-91e7-aa8f10dafb5a" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Triple Integral as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "252997ec-1b55-5df8-abca-04960f14c968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340126} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9bdc16-2200-503c-a8e6-00077d7d9907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340127} {:answer/id #uuid "9a047905-3474-5e53-8969-c3dbe12a8c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340128} {:answer/id #uuid "336958b9-64f3-526b-b3a4-9d5d363e5861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340129} {:answer/id #uuid "b179aff1-bd28-5e06-90ea-5a6c3e46c214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b179aff1-bd28-5e06-90ea-5a6c3e46c214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340130} :answer-field/id #uuid "18bd21b8-46eb-5d97-9f5c-43bc80f5dc15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2538bdad-281c-5cc7-951e-592c78afc26b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39478" :question/problem "Express the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{e}^{f}…\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340131 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d3a0d58-20a3-570d-91e7-aa8f10dafb5a" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Triple Integral as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9befddf-6db5-5d22-8f1c-c41b35f1f4ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340133} {:answer/id #uuid "19305c9f-184c-5c60-9bc9-401195516761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340134} {:answer/id #uuid "dde7a15c-28ae-5d15-b4fd-ba56a6c7a7ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340135} {:answer/id #uuid "d7642b6f-33c4-5dae-a332-34543185b158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 175921863